WEBVTT

00:00:03.195 --> 00:00:05.355
Hey, I think
that might be Shank.

00:00:05.515 --> 00:00:06.835
Listen up, mice...

00:00:06.995 --> 00:00:09.995
anyone who tries to play
with this cat's ride

00:00:10.115 --> 00:00:11.235
is gonna get got.

00:00:11.395 --> 00:00:13.915
JIMMY:
You're going down, Shank.

00:00:14.395 --> 00:00:16.795
Pyro.
Give those punks the works.

00:00:16.995 --> 00:00:18.475
With pleasure.

00:00:19.315 --> 00:00:20.955
(BOTH GASP)

00:00:21.515 --> 00:00:23.315
ANNOUNCER: End of the road!

00:00:23.475 --> 00:00:26.075
Gosh dang it!
Now we gotta start all over.

00:00:26.875 --> 00:00:28.155
Ralph, maybe...

00:00:28.235 --> 00:00:30.195
-(PANTING)
-Hey, where are you going?

00:00:30.355 --> 00:00:32.355
I am scared.

00:00:32.555 --> 00:00:33.635
If we get burned up in here,

00:00:33.715 --> 00:00:34.835
that's it, we're dead,
we're gone.

00:00:34.995 --> 00:00:36.555
So, I think we should
get outta here right now.

00:00:36.715 --> 00:00:39.115
No, wait, wait.
I have an idea.

00:00:39.355 --> 00:00:40.795
-(BELL RINGS)
-(POWER SWITCH CLANGS)

00:00:41.715 --> 00:00:42.875
Hey, Shank?

00:00:43.035 --> 00:00:44.275
What's up, Pyro?

00:00:44.435 --> 00:00:46.835
Um, do you ever reckon
we're going a bit too hard

00:00:46.915 --> 00:00:48.075
on the players?

00:00:48.275 --> 00:00:51.155
Honestly, no, I don't.

00:00:51.315 --> 00:00:55.395
Of course, I have empathy for
players like DirtySocks537

00:00:55.475 --> 00:00:57.475
and BabeRaham_Linkin...

00:00:58.155 --> 00:00:59.515
but if we just let them win,

00:00:59.595 --> 00:01:01.595
where's the life lesson?
You know?

00:01:01.675 --> 00:01:05.035
-PYRO: Mmm.
-Yeah, but to Pyro's point...

00:01:05.195 --> 00:01:07.675
I mean, those players
work so hard to get here.

00:01:07.835 --> 00:01:09.315
I hear you, Felony...

00:01:09.395 --> 00:01:11.395
but imagine a game
without challenges.

00:01:11.595 --> 00:01:14.595
The same predictable thing
every single time...

00:01:14.755 --> 00:01:15.795
who wants that?

00:01:15.955 --> 00:01:16.995
Shank's right.

00:01:17.155 --> 00:01:19.675
I just saw a really insightful
TED talk...

00:01:19.835 --> 00:01:21.915
and I can't really remember
what the guy said.

00:01:22.075 --> 00:01:23.955
It was more about
how he made me feel.

00:01:24.115 --> 00:01:26.275
But I think, ultimately,
the point was...

00:01:26.435 --> 00:01:29.435
I honor your journeys, guys.

00:01:29.595 --> 00:01:31.675
And we honor yours,
Butcher Boy.

00:01:31.835 --> 00:01:32.835
Thank you.

00:01:33.035 --> 00:01:33.995
Hey, Shank,

00:01:34.115 --> 00:01:35.435
did you ever wonder
what it would be like...

00:01:35.595 --> 00:01:37.315
if someone actually
did get your car?

00:01:37.475 --> 00:01:38.755
Well, I know one thing...

00:01:38.955 --> 00:01:41.635
whoever does will have to be
the best of the best.

00:01:41.715 --> 00:01:43.195
-(KNOCKS ON DOOR)
-(ALL EXCLAIM)

00:01:45.475 --> 00:01:47.035
Good day to you, madam.

00:01:47.195 --> 00:01:48.235
Who are you?

00:01:48.395 --> 00:01:51.435
I'm here from the,
uh, Department of Noise.

00:01:52.035 --> 00:01:54.235
And the thing is, we've been
getting some complaints

00:01:54.315 --> 00:01:55.715
down at HQ.

00:01:55.795 --> 00:01:57.555
Uh, Larry's the one
who takes the calls.

00:01:57.715 --> 00:01:58.915
Anyways, someone told Larry...

00:01:59.075 --> 00:02:00.115
that we've been
hearing a lot of

00:02:00.195 --> 00:02:01.675
gun sounds
and screaming sounds...

00:02:01.835 --> 00:02:03.635
and what-have-you.
That sort of thing.

00:02:03.795 --> 00:02:07.315
Whoa! This is nice.

00:02:08.435 --> 00:02:10.715
Where have you
been all my life?

00:02:11.355 --> 00:02:13.275
Uh, so I came to
check on things.

00:02:13.435 --> 00:02:15.315
Oh, I'm sorry, who did you
say you were again?

00:02:15.395 --> 00:02:17.075
Oh, I'm Larry?

00:02:17.475 --> 00:02:19.315
Uh, you said
Larry took the call.

00:02:19.395 --> 00:02:22.315
-(ENGINE REVVING)
-(TIRES SCREECHING)

00:02:23.355 --> 00:02:25.035
-(GROANS)
-(GASPS)

00:02:26.995 --> 00:02:28.795
Good job, Larry!

00:02:28.955 --> 00:02:31.435
Yeah, worked like a charm!

00:02:34.755 --> 00:02:36.995
(TIRES SCREECHING)

00:02:37.355 --> 00:02:39.275
Are you kidding me?
Someone got Shank's car?

00:02:39.435 --> 00:02:41.555
And I need yours. Sorry.

00:02:43.755 --> 00:02:45.835
I'm just... I'm just gonna go.

00:02:47.315 --> 00:02:48.435
(JIMMY CRIES)

00:02:48.515 --> 00:02:50.715
This is the worst day
of my life!

00:02:51.715 --> 00:02:53.595
(SIGHS) It's a shame
we have to leave so soon.

00:02:53.675 --> 00:02:55.035
This game is cool.

00:02:55.235 --> 00:02:56.235
Just get us out of here

00:02:56.315 --> 00:02:58.355
so we can get this car
to Spamley and get paid.

00:02:58.515 --> 00:02:59.675
No problem.

00:02:59.755 --> 00:03:01.675
(CARS CRASHING)

00:03:01.955 --> 00:03:03.035
RALPH: Uh-oh.

00:03:03.115 --> 00:03:05.195
VANELLOPE: Look at this guy
coming in hot.

00:03:15.995 --> 00:03:19.355
-(VANELLOPE SHRIEKS)
-(RALPH SHOUTING)

00:03:21.435 --> 00:03:24.195
You mess with the bull, you
get the horns, little girl!

00:03:24.915 --> 00:03:26.315
(RALPH SCREAMS)

00:03:28.475 --> 00:03:30.395
You still have value,
Butcher Boy.

00:03:33.595 --> 00:03:35.755
RALPH: Oh, no!
It's that Shank lady.

00:03:35.915 --> 00:03:37.035
She looks upset.

00:03:37.235 --> 00:03:39.275
Ah, don't worry,
I'll lose her.

00:03:39.515 --> 00:03:40.835
(RALPH YELLING)

00:03:41.195 --> 00:03:42.515
(TIRES SCREECHING)

00:03:45.915 --> 00:03:47.315
(RALPH SHOUTING)

00:03:48.075 --> 00:03:49.315
Where are you going?

00:03:49.475 --> 00:03:52.035
Kid, get back on the track.
I'm gonna lose my cookies.

00:03:52.195 --> 00:03:54.515
There is no track.
I can drive anywhere.

00:03:55.155 --> 00:03:56.395
Whoo!

00:04:02.155 --> 00:04:05.035
(RALPH SHOUTING)

00:04:09.355 --> 00:04:12.035
Oh, kid, she's coming up
right behind us.

00:04:12.235 --> 00:04:13.195
Oh, hello!

00:04:13.395 --> 00:04:15.235
I believe you have
something of mine.

00:04:15.395 --> 00:04:16.995
Yeah, come and get it.

00:04:17.555 --> 00:04:19.115
(ENGINE REVVING)

00:04:20.795 --> 00:04:22.315
(TIRES SCREECHING)

00:04:28.035 --> 00:04:30.355
-Ooh!
-(RALPH SHOUTING)

00:04:31.995 --> 00:04:34.035
(EXCLAIMS)
This girl can drive.

00:04:44.755 --> 00:04:46.195
Would you hurry up
and lose her?

00:04:46.395 --> 00:04:47.475
I'm trying!

00:04:49.035 --> 00:04:51.075
-Hang on, chumbo!
-(TIRES SCREECHING)

00:04:51.155 --> 00:04:52.515
(RALPH SHRIEKS)

00:04:54.595 --> 00:04:57.275
(RALPH SHOUTS, WHIMPERS)

00:04:57.355 --> 00:04:59.275
I don't like this!

00:05:00.875 --> 00:05:02.275
(RALPH GASPING)

00:05:02.355 --> 00:05:05.355
(RALPH EXCLAIMING)

00:05:08.595 --> 00:05:10.035
(TIRES SCREECHING)

00:05:10.715 --> 00:05:13.555
Whoa! Mother Hubbard,
this lady can really drive.

00:05:13.755 --> 00:05:15.675
Kid, fire!
Do you see the fire?

00:05:15.835 --> 00:05:16.835
Dead end! Dead end!

00:05:16.995 --> 00:05:19.595
Not for me. Bye-bye, Shanky.

00:05:19.675 --> 00:05:20.755
(DISTORTED SHOUTING)

00:05:21.035 --> 00:05:22.195
VANELLOPE: Whoo-hoo!

00:05:22.275 --> 00:05:23.995
RALPH: Oh, yeah!
VANELLOPE: That's the stuff.

00:05:24.075 --> 00:05:25.075
Good job, kid.

00:05:25.155 --> 00:05:27.835
Oh, yeah,
I feel like me again.

00:05:27.995 --> 00:05:29.155
One exit straight ahead.

00:05:36.595 --> 00:05:37.635
(TIRES SCREECHING)

